cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or benchmark, please cite this release."
title: "dense-solver for counting and matching in SAT"
type: software
version: "0.0.4"
authors:
  - given-names: Merlin
    family-names: Numa
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/libdense/dense-solver"
abstract: >-
  A C11 SAT solver with reusable sparse counting and Hall matching. The
  release includes 30 public SAT benchmarks, native solver comparisons,
  counting certificates, an independent checker and a reusable C library.
  Merlin Numa directed development using OpenAI ChatGPT and Anthropic Claude.
keywords:
  - Boolean satisfiability
  - pigeonhole principle
  - cardinality constraints
  - Hall matching
  - domino tiling
  - SAT solver
  - reproducible benchmarking

references:
